  "difficulty_reason": "The selected criterion requires a uniform hierarchy of reinforced bin growth under regularly varying reproduction laws. The proof extracts the random rank window from the full current configuration, bootstraps its conditional insertion intensity through all bins, and handles the critical slowly varying boundary and first frozen bin. This random-front asymptotic hierarchy exceeds ordinary doctoral probability qualifiers; Freedman conditional laws of large numbers and Karamata estimates are only precisely named prerequisites.",
